RGB888 configs without alpha on the Metal backend (ADR-0043 c4; ADR-0029, decision 8).

Why: GLSurfaceView's default config chooser (8, 8, 8, 0 and a depth of 16 or more) takes the first config
with exactly no alpha, which Android 15 lists first (RGB888, buffer size 24, EGL_NATIVE_VISUAL_ID
RGBX_8888). The Metal backend made only RGBA8888 configs, so every app on that chooser failed with "No
config chosen". Now DisplayMtl adds an RGB888 twin without alpha of every config, after them, so that the
RGBA8888 configs keep their IDs, with GL_RGB8 as the render target format and no RGBA texture binding.
SurfaceMtl gives their surfaces B8G8R8X8, which the format table stores as BGRA8Unorm with ANGLE's emulated
alpha: the window's drawables get the write mask without alpha that offscreen textures of that format get
already, and clears write alpha 1. So alpha reads 1, as on Android: after a clear or a draw with less, and
for GL_DST_ALPHA; GL_ALPHA_BITS is 0.
Upstream: could go upstream; the Vulkan backend lists GL_RGB8 configs on Android (DisplayVkAndroid.cpp).
Remove: when upstream's Metal backend lists configs without alpha.

diff --git a/src/libANGLE/renderer/metal/DisplayMtl.mm b/src/libANGLE/renderer/metal/DisplayMtl.mm
--- a/src/libANGLE/renderer/metal/DisplayMtl.mm
+++ b/src/libANGLE/renderer/metal/DisplayMtl.mm
@@ -632,6 +632,24 @@
         config.depthSize   = GetDepthSize(config.depthStencilFormat);
         config.stencilSize = GetStencilSize(config.depthStencilFormat);
         configs.add(config);
+    }
+
+    // Minato (patch 0006): an RGB888 twin without alpha of every config, as Android lists one first for
+    // GLSurfaceView's default chooser (8, 8, 8, 0). SurfaceMtl keeps its surfaces' alpha at 1. The twins come
+    // last, so the RGBA8888 configs keep their IDs.
+    std::vector<egl::Config> twins;
+    for (const auto &entry : configs)
+    {
+        egl::Config twin        = entry.second;
+        twin.alphaSize          = 0;
+        twin.bufferSize         = twin.redSize + twin.greenSize + twin.blueSize;
+        twin.renderTargetFormat = GL_RGB8;
+        twin.bindToTextureRGBA  = EGL_FALSE;
+        twins.push_back(twin);
+    }
+    for (const egl::Config &twin : twins)
+    {
+        configs.add(twin);
     }
 
     return configs;
